{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Its horns</b> — Three times in the Masorah: this one, and the other two: אשר נתן ה׳ חכמה ותבונה בהמה (Exodus 31:6), כי בהמה שמן חלקו (Isaiah 5:17). This is what is written: the wisdom gives life to its possessors (Ecclesiastes 7:12). חכמה ותבונה בהמה — כי בהמה שמן חלקו. And furthermore, that it raises him and elevates him, as written: לשאת אותו בהמה (Numbers 4:32)."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The verse references in parentheses are not in the original; they are omitted per discipline. The word בהמה here carries a double sense: in our verse it means 'its horns' (ב + המה), while in the other two verses it means 'beast/cattle.' The juxtaposition argument turns on this dual reading."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:14:46.660327331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}